    "body": "## Motivation\n\nFixes #43162. `--dtype float32` (and its alias `\"float\"`) are advertised, parser-accepted choices, but no FlashInfer attention kernel exists for fp32: the JIT module URI map (`filename_safe_dtype_map` in `flashinfer.jit.utils`) covers fp16/bf16/fp8/integer dtypes only. The engine loads the weights, enters CUDA-graph capture, and dies with a bare `KeyError: torch.float32` from `get_batch_decode_uri`, taking the whole process group down with an unactionable message.\n\n## Modifications\n\n`FlashInferAttnBackend.__init__` now validates the resolved model dtype before touching any runner state and raises a `ValueError` that names the supported dtypes and points at `--dtype float16/bfloat16` or `--attention-backend torch_native`. Same failure class as before, but raised at backend init instead of mid-capture, with the remediation in the message.\n\nNew CPU unit tests pin the gate, the message content, and that backend construction raises before reading any pool/config state.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNo model output path changes; the gate only rejects a configuration that never produced output.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nN/A; one dict-free tuple membership check at backend construction.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit). (`pre-commit run` on both files, all hooks pass)\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests). (3 tests + subtests, registered for base-a-test-cpu)\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations). (the argument and its help text stay valid for backends with fp32 support)\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed). (N/A, see above)\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n## To verify\n\nLocal verification was CPU-only: the new tests pass against the fix and fail when the gate is neutralized (red-green). I have no local GPU, so the fp32-plus-FlashInfer incompatibility itself is asserted from FlashInfer's JIT dispatch source, and the end-to-end engine startup path is left to CI.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #37919588264](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37919588264)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37919587857](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37919587857)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #37919588141](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37919588141)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
